y Citation]\n  * Zero-sum subsequences in bounded-sum $\\{-1, 1\\}$-sequences\n\nYair Caro, Adriana Hansberg, Amanda Montejano\n\nDec 21 2016 math.CO math.NT arXiv:1612.06523v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{1612.06523, author = {Yair Caro and Adriana Hansberg and Amanda Montejano}, title = {{Z}ero-sum subsequences in bounded-sum $\\{-1, 1\\}$-sequences}, year = {2016}, eprint = {1612.06523}, note = {arXiv:1612.06523v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nThe following result gives the flavor of this paper: Let $t$, $k$ and $q$ be integers such that $q\\geq 0$, $0\\leq t < k$ and $t \\equiv k \\,({\\rm mod}\\, 2)$, and let $s\\in [0,t+1]$ be the unique integer satisfying $s \\equiv q + \\frac{k-t-2}{2} \\,({\\rm mod} \\, (t+2))$. Then for any integer $n$ such that \\[n \\ge \\max\\left{k,\\frac12(t+2)k^2 + \\fracq-st+2k - \\fract2 + s\\right}\\]and any function $f:[n]\\to \\{-1,1\\}$ with $|\\sum_{i=1}^nf(i)| \\le q$, there is a set $B \\subseteq [n]$ of $k$ consecutive integers with $|\\sum_{y\\in B}f(y)| \\le t$. Moreover, this bound is sharp for all the parameters involved and a characterization of the extremal sequences is given. This and other similar results involving different subsequences are presented, including decompositions of sequences into subsequences of bounded weight.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Toth_L in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3AToth_L+in%3Amath)\nciteturn0search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Nov 11 2016 math.GR math.CO math.NT arXiv:1611.03302v1 ... @misc{1611.03302, author = {László Tóth}, title = {{T}he number of subgroups of the group $\\{B}bb{{Z}}_m\\times \\{B}bb{{Z}}_n \\times \\{B}bb{{Z}}_r \\times \\{B}bb{{Z}}_s$}, year = {2016}, eprint = {1611.03302}, note = {arXiv:1611.03302v1} }[Button: Copy Citation] ... We introduce and study the concept of cyclicity degree of a finite group $G$. This quantity measures the probability o