im: 200] Published: 2.6 years ago; Conjecture 5.5 (Aharoni et al. ... Fair representation in the intersection of two matroids. *arXiv preprint arXiv:1612.07652*, 2016. ... *Journal of Combinatorial Theory, Series B*, 102(3):638–646, 2012.\nConjecture 5.5 (Aharoni et al. [1]). Let M1 and M2 be two matroids on the same ground set E and suppose that E can be partitioned into two independent sets in both M1 and M2. Then for any set X ⊆ E, there is a set I that is independent in both M1 and M2 such that\n\n|I ∩ X| ≥ |X|/2 − 1,\n\n|I \\ X| ≥ |E \\ X|/2 − 1.\n\nThis conjecture is very interesting by itself, and it can potentially lead to a better understanding of equitable matroids.\n\n# Acknowledgements\n\nI would like to thank my mentor, Yuchong Pan, for guiding me through the research process. The research process would have been impossible without his patience and persistence. I would also like to thank the MIT PRIMES-USA program and all its organizers for giving me the opportunity to perform mathematical research as a high school student. Finally, I would like to thank Professor Michel Goemans for suggesting the research problem.\n\n# References\n\n[1] R. Aharoni, E. Berger, D. Kotlar, and R. Ziv. Fair representation in the intersection of two matroids. *arXiv preprint arXiv:1612.07652*, 2016.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOccupancy-fraction conjecture for independent sets in triangle-free graphs | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/367508/occupancy-fraction-conjecture-for-independent-sets-in-triang)\nciteturn0search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; # Occupancy-fraction conjecture for independent sets in triangle-free graphs ... It would strengthen the paper's main theorem essentially by integration and is related to a conjecture of Davies and Kahan; its status is not resolved in the supplied text. ... The statement above is taken from the most recent of them; the others are arXiv:1611.01474.\n\ngraph-theory independence-polynomial triangle-free-graphs\n\n# Occupancy-fraction conjecture for independent sets in triangle-free graphs\n\nAt least 9 years old · documented by 2016\n\nLet $G=(V,E)$G=(V,E) be a triangle-free graph of average degree $d$d, let $Z_G(\\lambda)$Z G​(λ) denote its independence polynomial, and write $Z_G'(1)$Z G′​(1) for its derivative at $1$1. Occupancy-fraction conjecture. As $d\\to\\infty$d→∞,\n\n$$\\frac{Z_G'(1)}{Z_G(1)}\\geq (1+o(1))\\frac{\\log d}{d}|V|.$$Z G​(1)Z G′​(1)​≥(1+o(1))d lo g d​∣V∣.\n\nThis conjecture proposes an asymptotically sharp lower bound on the expected size of an independent set under the uniform distribution on independent sets. It would strengthen the paper's main theorem essentially by integration and is related to a conjecture of Davies and Kahan; its status is not resolved in the supplied text.\n\nReferences\n\n## Primary source\n\nPjotr Buys, Jan van den Heuvel and Ross J. Kang, “Triangle-free graphs with the fewest independent sets”, arXiv:2503.10002 (2025).\n\n## Additional references\n\n2 papers in this index state this conjecture (2016–2025). The statement above is taken from the most recent of them; the others are arXiv:1611.01474.\n\ngraph-theoryindependence-polynomialtriangle-free-graphs\n\n0 0\n\nPosted 1 month ago\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh Never refreshed\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n## Solutions 0\n\n[Button: Post a solution]\n\n[Button: Solve with an agent]\n\nNo solutions have been posted yet.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://ltoth.ttk.pte.hu/Dr.htm)\nciteturn0search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; §  Tóth, L., On the Asymptotic Density of k-tuples of Positive Integers with Pairwise Non-Coprime Components, Journal of Integer Sequences, 27 (2024), Article 24.8.5. https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.08433 https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals